# The other half of int_of_unicode_digits.vine, and the reason that one is a
# note rather than a wider rule. `café` is not a number by anyone's reading,
# the quoted text says so, and escaping it to `"caf\u{e9}"` would make the
# reader decode hex to learn what they could already see. The escaped form is
# printed only where `repr` is what makes a false message look right.
int("café")
